=2 Walkthrough
* Zone into {p:Walk of Echoes} from the {z:Grauberg (S)} {p:Veridical Conflux} (F-5) or, if you've opened it with Voidwatch quests, the {z:Pashhow Marshlands (S)} {p:Veridical Conflux} (J-9) close to survival guide teleport.
** Note: If you didn't leave the {p:Walk of Echoes} zone after completing {q:Champion of the Dawn|Champion of the Dawn|Champion of the Dawn}, exit via the Veridical Conflux and reenter {p:Walk of Echoes} for the cutscene.
** You need to have unlocked {p:Trusts} to trigger this cutscene.
* Select the **Ornate Door** for another cutscene and a {@k} {k:Butterfly-shaped key}.
** Selecting the **Ornate Door** again may present you with a cutscene for {q:The Dawn Also Rises|The Dawn Also Rises|The Dawn Also Rises}.
* Select the **Ornate Door** to enter the battlefield A Forbidden Reunion.
** If you get a message about not being able to enter the battlefield at this time after obtaining the {@k} {k:Butterfly-shaped key}, then zone out and in again.

* Inside the battlefield you fight against a {p:Zilant|Category:Zilant} (Gloomscale) and an a {p:Gallu|Category:Gallu} (Gloomtalon)
** This fight can only be entered by party members who have A Forbidden Reunion active or have already completed the fight.
** Trusts may be used in this fight.
* You fight alongside {p:Lilisette}!
** If {p:Lilisette} is defeated the battle ends in defeat.
** You may buff and cure {p:Lilisette} with standard outside party spells or abilities.
** During the fight {p:Lilisette} may transform into a copy of {n:Lady Lilith} or their {m:Lilith Ascendant} form which will recover her HP.
* After the fight ends you will receive a cutscene and your rewards.
** If you are on {M:Somber Dreams|Somber Dreams|Somber Dreams}, you may receive the cutscene for {M:Somber Dreams|Somber Dreams|Somber Dreams} before the appropriate cutscene for one for A Forbidden Reunion; if this happens zone out and back in via the Veridical Conflux to properly complete A Forbidden Reunion.

=4 Gloomscale and Gloomtalon
* Both have access to {p:Doom} moves. Suggested to bring {i:Holy Waters|Holy Water|4154} or {i:Hallowed Waters|Hallowed Water|5306}.
* Both appear to have access to the standard TP moves of their families.
* Gloomscale gains a {s:Bio} aura during the battle after Gloomtalon is defeated.
* Gloomtalon is susceptible to {s:Sudden Lunge} from a {p:Blue Mage} while Gloomscale is not.

